From: Filipe Manana <fdmanana@suse.com>
Date: Thu, 11 Jun 2026 15:16:21 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] btrfs: fix root leak if its reloc root is unexpected in
 merge_reloc_roots()
Git-commit: ce6050bafb4e33377dc17fcc357736bfc351180c
Patch-mainline: v7.2-rc4
References: CVE-2026-68422 bsc#1274706

If we have an unexpected reloc_root for our root, we jump to the out label
but never drop the reference we obtained for root, resulting in a leak.
Add a missing btrfs_put_root() call.

Fixes: 24213fa46c70 ("btrfs: do proper error handling in merge_reloc_roots")
Reviewed-by: Qu Wenruo <wqu@suse.com>
Reviewed-by: Johannes Thumshirn <johannes.thumshirn@wdc.com>
Signed-off-by: Filipe Manana <fdmanana@suse.com>
Reviewed-by: David Sterba <dsterba@suse.com>
Signed-off-by: David Sterba <dsterba@suse.com>
---
 fs/btrfs/relocation.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/fs/btrfs/relocation.c b/fs/btrfs/relocation.c
index fb85bc8b345c7..9447d009a9a0e 100644
--- a/fs/btrfs/relocation.c
+++ b/fs/btrfs/relocation.c
@@ -1912,6 +1912,7 @@ again:
 				 * corruption, e.g. bad reloc tree key offset.
 				 */
 				ret = -EINVAL;
+				btrfs_put_root(root);
 				goto out;
 			}
 			ret = merge_reloc_root(rc, root);
-- 
2.35.3

